{"c":[{"id":"ea5143bf5e6179f1","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger over all windows charges a text to every window showing it; kindless fill fields withheld only on related cuts; live Jev replays vary about 3 fields, rerun before trusting a delta; socket tests bind publish to that test's own HelperServer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"15d4fcad6f30cb62","sum":"SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() charges a taken text to every window showing it, either way round, and refuses if any is over budget; a kindless fill field is withheld only on cuts of typed values or its label words, never on any cut (B13).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075125Z-769f076b2b26d50b","text":"SnippetLedger(windows) charges a taken text to every window that shows it, either way round (line inside the text, or text inside a line); refuses when any of them is over budget. Build it over model.windows.values(), never just the source window (B13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T075154Z-10f895f4b8d309e7","text":"A fill field whose label names no kind is withheld when a cut took a typed value or a cut conversation left out a line sharing its label words; withholding it on any cut blanked Name on the fill desk (unrelated team chat always cut) and lost the first-look offer (B13 live-final).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"be073912f9f26071","sum":"Live Jev replays vary by about 3 fields run to run (24-27 of 78, B13): rerun before reading a delta. Socket tests bind publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, or a late 'stopped' leaks into the next test (B14).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075211Z-5ac7a437648ff4d5","text":"Live replay noise: the same code gave 24, 26, 27 and 25 of 78 on 'sources in Messages' rule on (B13); pre-ask withholding is deterministic, so differences under about 3 fields are Jev answering differently. Rerun part with --variants/--rules/--fixes before reading a delta.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100918Z-34fd442f4a978ffa","text":"Socket test harnesses must bind the helper's publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, not the reassigned server variable: an earlier test's run timed out 5 s later and its 'stopped id-1' reached a later test's host (B13's flake, fixed B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d2825e282ce0f8d","sum":"B14: load-proof tests pin the generator clock (setGeneratorClock(() => 0)); names withheld only on namesCut; a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (zod union on phase); dry-run live replays with an oracle-Jev copy of live-replay.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (find exposed ones with a wall clock jumping 1 s per read); a name field is withheld only on namesCut, since counting names prose mentions blanked Full name on Messages sets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase); before a live replay, run a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
